FILE = "gta-6-why-its-a-big-deal.html"
TITLE = "GTA 6, decoded: why one video game has the whole world counting down"
TAG = "Flavor Decoded"
H1 = "GTA 6, decoded"
DEK = "Thirteen years, two delays and a predecessor that out-earned Hollywood's biggest films. Why Thursday's release is about more than gaming."
META = "Flavor Decoded · 17 Nov 2026 · 6 min read"
LEAD = ("img/gta6-lead.jpg", "Jason and Lucia, the two leads of Grand Theft Auto VI", "Rockstar Games, via @canaltradicional__ / Instagram")

BODY = [
("p", "If your feed has been full of neon palm trees, a couple in bandanas and a countdown clock lately, you've already met it. Grand Theft Auto VI comes out on Thursday, 19 November, on PS5 and Xbox Series X|S. For people who play games, it's the release they've waited more than a decade for. For everyone else, it's a fair question: why is one video game being treated like a World Cup final?"),
("p", "The short answer is money, time and a fan base that never went away. Here's the longer one."),

("h2", "01 · The series", "A game you know ", "even if you've never played it"),
("p", "Grand Theft Auto is Rockstar Games' open-world crime series. You drive, steal, take on missions and wander a satirical copy of an American city that seems to go on forever. The last main game, GTA V, came out on 17 September 2013 for the PlayStation 3 and Xbox 360. It was the first main entry since GTA IV in 2008."),
("p", "Since then, GTA V has been sold again on two more generations of consoles, and people have kept buying it. That long tail is a big part of why its sequel matters so much."),

("h2", "02 · The record", "$1 billion ", "in three days"),
("p", "GTA V sold 11.21 million copies on its first day and brought in $815.7 million. Three days after launch it passed $1 billion. Guinness World Records named it the fastest entertainment property ever to reach that mark. Call of Duty: Black Ops II had needed 15 days, and blockbuster films like Avatar and The Avengers were slower too."),
("p", "Then it simply kept going. In its results on 9 November 2026, Take-Two Interactive, which owns Rockstar, said GTA V has now sold nearly 235 million copies. For years it has added about 5 million copies every three months, a pace most brand-new games would be happy with. That's the bar GTA VI walks in against."),
("img", "img/gta6-logo.jpg", "The Grand Theft Auto VI logo, first shown in the December 2023 trailer.", "Rockstar Games, via @rockstargames / Instagram"),

("h2", "03 · The wait", "Thirteen years ", "and two delays"),
("p", "The first trailer, in December 2023, promised a 2025 release. In May 2025 Rockstar pushed the game to 26 May 2026. Then on 6 November 2025 it moved again, to 19 November 2026, saying the extra months would let it finish the game with the polish players expect. That was the last change. Take-Two repeated the date at every earnings call since, and the launch trailer on 15 October 2026 confirmed it once more."),
("p", "Thirteen years between main games is a lifetime in this business. Kids who played GTA V at 12 are now adults with their own consoles and their own money, and that's a big part of the crowd lining up this week."),

("h2", "04 · The hype", "Records broken ", "before release"),
("p", "The first trailer leaked, so Rockstar put it out early. It pulled 90,421,491 YouTube views in 24 hours, and Guinness World Records recognised three records from it: the most-viewed video game reveal on YouTube in a day, the most-liked game trailer on YouTube with 8.9 million likes, and the most-viewed non-music YouTube video in 24 hours. That last one had belonged to MrBeast. Only BTS's \"Butter\" video has done more in a single day."),
("p", "The second trailer, released in May 2025, went further. Rockstar said it was watched 475 million times across all platforms in its first 24 hours, more than the trailers for Deadpool &amp; Wolverine and Spider-Man: No Way Home."),
("img", "img/gta6-bandanas.jpg", "Jason and Lucia in official GTA VI artwork.", "Rockstar Games, via @sucumba.games / Instagram"),
("p", "Pre-orders opened on 25 June 2026, and Take-Two has been unusually open about how they're going. It hasn't shared a number, but in August chief executive Strauss Zelnick put it like this:"),
("quote", "The level of preorders is unprecedented and astonishing, and we're grateful for that.", "Strauss Zelnick, Take-Two CEO, August 2026"),
("p", "In November he said they were still running well above the company's own expectations. Take-Two expects $8 billion to $8.2 billion in net bookings for the year to March 2027, a forecast built around GTA VI's launch. Other publishers have spent the past year moving their own releases out of its way."),

("h2", "05 · The game", "Back to ", "Vice City"),
("p", "GTA VI is set in Leonida, Rockstar's version of Florida, with Vice City, its long-running stand-in for Miami, at the centre. The series made its name there with 2002's Grand Theft Auto: Vice City, and last went back in 2006's Vice City Stories on the PSP. Rockstar has named six regions so far: Vice City, the Leonida Keys, Grassrivers, Port Gellhorn, Ambrosia and Mount Kalaga National Park."),
("p", "The story follows two leads, Jason Duval and Lucia Caminos, who are a couple. Rockstar's own description says they've always known the deck is stacked against them, and the trailers have leaned hard on the relationship."),
("img", "img/gta6-car.jpg", "Jason and Lucia on the official cover art for Grand Theft Auto VI.", "Rockstar Games, via @gamefirstfr / Instagram"),

("h2", "06 · The price", "$80, ", "and no disc"),
("p", "The standard edition costs $79.99 and the Ultimate Edition $99.99. That's $10 more than the $70 that had become normal for big console games, and the industry is watching to see whether others follow. Boxed copies carry a download code instead of a disc."),
("p", "Digital copies could be pre-loaded from 12 November. The game unlocks at midnight local time on 19 November, based on the region set on your PlayStation or Xbox account rather than where you're standing. It's console-only for now, with no PC version announced, and at launch it's a single-player game. There's no new online mode yet."),

("h2", "07 · The point", "Why it reaches ", "past gamers"),
("p", "Strip away the trailers and the countdowns, and GTA VI is a test of how big a single piece of entertainment can get. Its predecessor beat the biggest films in history to $1 billion, and is still selling thirteen years later. This one arrives with more attention, a higher price and a bigger audience than anything else in games."),
("p", "Whether it lives up to all that is a question for Thursday and the weeks after it. But if you've wondered why your timeline went neon, now you know."),
]

